.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Defines the structural layout and behavioral contract of a custom floating‑point format\&. Implementations describe how a binary floating‑point number is encoded into sign, exponent, and mantissa fields, including exponent bias, hidden bit rules, and total bit width\&. 

\fBIFloat<TSelf, TBias>\fP abstracts the representation of non‑IEEE floating formats such as \fR\fBHalf16\fP\fP, \fR\fBHalf16b\fP\fP, \fRBFloat16\fP, or any other custom 16‑bit or N‑bit float\&. It provides: 

.PP
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
Structural metadata (bit counts, bias, hidden bit)\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
Field extraction (sign, exponent, mantissa)\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
Classification (zero, infinity, NaN, subnormal, normal, integer)\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
Arithmetic operations (add, multiply, divide, unary ops)\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
Comparison operators and ordering semantics\&.   
.IP "\(bu" 2
Serialization support via \fBIByteSerializable<TSelf>\fP\&.   
.PP

.PP
Implementations must be \fRstruct\fP types and self‑referential (\fITSelf\fP )\&. This ensures value‑type semantics and prevents boxing during arithmetic or comparison operations\&. 
.PP
\fBType Constraints\fP
.TP
\fITSelf\fP : \fIstruct\fP
.TP
\fITSelf\fP : \fI\fBIFloat\fP\fP
.TP
\fITSelf\fP : \fITSelf\fP
.TP
\fITSelf\fP : \fITBias\fP
.PP
